{
  "title": "Five-part leukocyte entropy does not improve nonlinear CRP prediction across NHANES survey cycles",
  "abstract": "In 4,122 NHANES 2005\u20132006 and 4,927 separately sampled 2007\u20132008 adults, adding leukocyte Shannon entropy to nonlinear differential-count and demographic/adiposity measures increased target log-CRP MSE by 0.000334 (0.031%). The source-refit/target-PSU 95% interval [-0.000887, 0.005506] spans benefit and harm; this exploratory analysis provides no robust evidence of added predictive utility.",
  "keywords": [
    "leukocyte entropy",
    "CRP",
    "NHANES",
    "temporal transfer",
    "negative result"
  ],
